<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Lorde returns three weeks after her first visit here. She saw Dr. Lozano of medical oncology this morning. She has taken tamoxifen every day for five months. She has three or four hot flashes a day and is woken by one on one or two nights a week; she would rather manage them without another medicine if she can. Her periods continue every four to five weeks, a little lighter, with no bleeding between them. She has no leg swelling, chest pain, or breathlessness. The mastectomy scar is comfortable, and she has no arm heaviness or swelling. She is writing and walking daily and feels steady in mood. She is settled in her decisions after surgery: she chose a flat closure and does not want reconstruction or an external prosthesis. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Medical oncology consultation this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Tamoxifen</td><td>Five months, taken daily</td></tr><tr><td>Vasomotor symptoms</td><td>Three or four hot flashes a day; wakes one or two nights a week</td></tr><tr><td>Gynecologic</td><td>Periods every four to five weeks; no intermenstrual bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Arm and chest wall</td><td>No swelling, heaviness, or pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

