    <td>Invasive ductal carcinoma of the upper outer quadrant of the right breast, stage IA (pT1c pN0(sn) M0), grade 2, estrogen and progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative, recurrence score 14; treated by right total mastectomy with sentinel node biopsy and on adjuvant tamoxifen; synthetic modern counterpart of the documented 1978 breast cancer and mastectomy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>C50.411</td><td>S — Synthetic tumor details and treatment; the diagnosis and the mastectomy are documented (D), but no tumor details from her lifetime are used.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Estrogen receptor positive status of the breast cancer (ER 90 percent, PR 60 percent)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z17.0</td><td>S — Synthetic receptor result; no receptor status from her lifetime is known.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Absence of the right breast after mastectomy with flat closure; she chose not to have reconstruction and not to wear an external prosthesis</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z90.11</td><td>S — Synthetic coding of the documented mastectomy; the decision about a prosthesis echoes her documented choice and is respected as her own.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Long-term use of tamoxifen as adjuvant endocrine therapy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z79.810</td><td>S — Synthetic treatment status.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

